UnitCustomFeeModule::constructor
└── given a freshly deployed module
    └── it should set factory to the provided factory address

UnitCustomFeeModule::setCustomFee
├── when the caller is not the fee manager
│   └── it should revert with NotFeeManager
└── when the caller is the fee manager
    ├── when the fee exceeds the max fee and is not the zero indicator
    │   └── it should revert with FeeTooHigh
    └── when the fee is within the cap or the zero indicator
        ├── when the pool is not a registered pool
        │   └── it should revert with InvalidPool
        └── when the pool is a registered pool
            ├── it should set the custom fee
            └── it should emit SetCustomFee

UnitCustomFeeModule::getFee
├── when a zero fee has been explicitly set
│   └── it should return zero
├── when a positive fee has been set
│   └── it should return the custom fee
└── when no fee has been set
    └── it should revert with NoCustomFee
